    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382-a7">

                <pb facs="0620" n="550" xml:id="pg550"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vera Cruz,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 30, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Affairs here remain unchanged. The siege of Vera Cruz is still in progress, with
                    but little prospect of its speedy termination.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * *</p>
                <p>Those who are not interested here in the empire are anxious to know what view the
                    United States will take of the enlistment of men for the empire in Havana. As
                    stated in a previous letter, the first instalment has arrived, and the English
                    steamer from Havana, now due, is expected to bring more. Spain cannot protest if
                    the United States allow enlistments for the liberal army, or the fitting out of
                    privateers under the same flag, for the capture of the imperial gunboat
                    Tabasco.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * *</p>
            </div>
        </body>
